<title>INDIA: India's forex reserves rise to $23.58 bln on Nov 1.</title>
<headline>India's forex reserves rise to $23.58 bln on Nov 1.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.58 billion on November 1, 1996, from $23.50 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					   Nov 1	Oct 25	  Nov 3</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,126	19,015	 17,451</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,382	 4,410	  4,408</p>
<p>    SDRs				    76	    75	     29</p>
<p>    Total			     23,584	23,500	 21,888</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
